CORE gcc-only
main.c
--arch riscv64 --full-slice
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^not slicing, as the program contains inline assembly that may change any reachable object$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 37 heap object reachable from static: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 38 pointer in static: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line 39 pointers are restricted to known values: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line 50 escaped local of caller: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line 51 local without address: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line 59 heap object reachable from operand: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line 60 unreachable heap object: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
dereference failure.*: FAILURE$
--
The full slicer does not know which objects havoc_reachable changes and
reads, and therefore does not slice such programs.
